  "theorem": "There are explicit complex projective K3 surfaces admitting purely non-symplectic automorphisms tau of order four whose divisor lattices contain a tau-stable index-two or index-four copy of U+D4(-1)^2+A1(-1)^2.  The restricted Picard involution is integrally conjugate to the archived H10/45 action.  Its 59-root divisor-subsystem chamber therefore has the certified finite-volume noncompact 45-facet fixed Coxeter section in H10.  The displayed Weierstrass automorphism sigma supplies the Hodge action; tau is its Weyl conjugate furnished on the same surface by strong Torelli.",
